# Chapter01 Selenium general
Demonstrates basic Selenium features and Java methods, using Hamcrest matcher and JUnit as a testing framework

## project_A Minimum lines to open Browser Types & uses manual JAR import for dependency resolution & hard coded Driver locations
## project_B Demonstrates Selenium with Java methods (time, Loops, lambda expressions) & uses POM for dependency resolution & hard coded Driver locations
## project_C Demonstrates Hamcrest as a matcher
## project_D Demonstrates Junit5 @Before @Test

### Convention & Configuration
Convention:
IntelliJ IDE
QA desktop folder with sub-folders for projectShare(/resource) & projectTools(/Java)
Local WebDriver created with no access modifiers (i.e. leave blank so that it is 'Protected', without stating Private or Public)

Configuration:
Driver Location hard coded in repository
Dependencies resolved manually and by Maven (Selenium4, Junit 5 & Hamcrest)




